      "message": "don\u0027t you run into the same problem here?\nmux task (et. al.) indirectly call perform_mux_set() which gets us here\nand we still have a race condition because the flag is set after the\nINIT operation.\n\nat the same time, restart_tc_sm can call usb_mux_init() directly,\npotentially from a different task.\n\ncan the global usb_mux_init() simply clear USB_MUX_FLAG_INIT,\nthen rely on perform_mux_set to call an unlocked version of this\nusb_mux_init()? i think perform_mux_set() is guaranteed to run\nin the same thread, no additional locks needed.\n\nexit_low_power_mode() and similar functions that check\nUSB_MUX_FLAG_INIT become simpler.\nusb_mux_task() may need to do an initial perform_mux_set()\nso we still have the startup/boot scenario handled.",
